Lesson : What is STXT
    Number of lesson: 2/5
    Introduction >>
        **STXT** is a format (or language)
        for indented-based documents.
        The indentation makes the jerarquia of
        the document. 
        
        This is not XML. This is not YAML.
        The more close is XML, as you have nodes,
        namespaces and schemas. And at the surface
        it looks like some sort of YAML. But this
        is a diferent language.

        There are 2 types of nodes: **Inline and Block**

    Inline node: after ':' all is the value of the node

    Block node >>
        All the content of
        the block node is raw text.
        No escape chars, all the content
        is "as is".
        You can put whatever you like.

        A block node inside a block?
        Block node inside >>
            NOOO!! Inside 'Block node'
            all is text. No rules here.
            No more blocks here.

    Another node: You can have all the nodes you want
        Inner node: This is a child of 'Another node'
        Inner node: You can repeat the name 'Inner node'
